{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon","id":1381944,"title":"Heroic spirits in Typemoon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-16T10:23:58-07:00","id":1381944,"title":"Heroic spirits in Typemoon?","content":"Hello everyone, so do you know the thing most similar to Heroic Spirits?<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://typemoon.fandom.com/wiki/Heroic_Spirit\" target=\"_blank\">https://typemoon.fandom.com/wiki/Heroic_Spirit</a><br /> <br /> To be simple, Heroic Spirits are spirits of heroes who achieved great deeds in life, having become objects of worship after their deaths.<br /> <br /> The closet thing I find is Ancestor Spirits, but they are also different from this. Does anybody have more ideas? Had you fanmade rules for this? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-16-2020, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T20:10:30-07:00","id":1382044,"title":"","content":"The Throne of Heroes is much more the sort of thing you'd find in Mage. Its more the sort of thing of the High Umbra and its wierdness. I would just straight up port them to such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T22:59:08-07:00","id":1382066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382044#post1382044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Throne of Heroes is much more the sort of thing you'd find in Mage. Its more the sort of thing of the High Umbra and its wierdness. I would just straight up port them to such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well sorry but why?<br /> <br /> to be honest the first thing I thought about is they are very similiar to Ancestor Spirits<br /> <br /> And I think the Throne of Heroes or anywhere all heroic spirits reside is something like the Legendary Realm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T23:37:16-07:00","id":1382070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382066#post1382066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well sorry but why?<br /> <br /> to be honest the first thing I thought about is they are very similiar to Ancestor Spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't really. Your ancestor spirit is your ancestor spirit. If someone believes your ancestor is a Vampire that has no effect on how they are summoned. But Lets look at Vlad Tepes. He can be summoned as the a Lancer<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think the Throne of Heroes or anywhere all heroic spirits reside is something like the Legendary Realm </div> </div> </div>The throne of heroes is not a realm like the legendary Realm. Camelot would be a Legendary Realm. Uruk would be a Legendary Realm. David or Solomon's Israel would be a legendary Realm.<br /> <br /> The throne of heroes is much closer to the library of Alexandria or the Rivers of language. Its a place where the idealization of heroes are carved. Its not a place where King arthur hangs out with Gligamesh but rather a place where you can call an aspect of their concept from.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:36:40-07:00","id":1382081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382070#post1382070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They aren't really. Your ancestor spirit is your ancestor spirit. If someone believes your ancestor is a Vampire that has no effect on how they are summoned. But Lets look at Vlad Tepes. He can be summoned as the a Lancer</div> </div> </div> </div>But the origin of ancestor spirits also varies, some say they're spirits of dead garou, others say they're memories of mates<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382070#post1382070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The throne of heroes is much closer to the library of Alexandria or the Rivers of language. Its a place where the idealization of heroes are carved. Its not a place where King arthur hangs out with Gligamesh but rather a place where you can call an aspect of their concept from.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> W20 Umbra,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shapeshifters exert significant influence over the Umbra as a consequence of their half-spirit natures, and the Legendary Realm is a manifestation of their songs and stories of the past deeds, great heroes, and epic battles of their kind. </div> </div> </div>Legendary Realm also has ideas,<br /> <br /> iirc, many spirits are manifestation of ideas or thoughts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T12:41:42-07:00","id":1382224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382081#post1382081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the origin of ancestor spirits also varies, some say they're spirits of dead garou, others say they're memories of mates</div> </div> </div> </div>The second option is not really one that W:tA gives much stock to, or should. There are plenty of games that try to build up an ironic situation where ghosts aren't ghosts and everything is belief, such as Mage or Shadowrun, but W:tA is not one of them. Beyond that, the Middle Umbra to which Garou and Fera are connected is actually pretty grounded and doesn't really go in for wild fancies of belief; it is, in fact, the cornerstone of physical reality in Werewolf's particular version of animism, as the ephemera of the Middle Umbra determines what is real and what is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> W20 Umbra,<br /> <br /> Legendary Realm also has ideas,<br /> <br /> iirc, many spirits are manifestation of ideas or thoughts </div> </div> </div>Everything in the Legendary Realm is an emanation of the Realm, though, not a spirit. As a general rule, emanations can't leave their home Near Realm; to brave and do so anyway causes them to cease to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T11:32:28-07:00","id":1382359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382224#post1382224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second option is not really one that W:tA gives much stock to, or should. There are plenty of games that try to build up an ironic situation where ghosts aren't ghosts and everything is belief, such as Mage or Shadowrun, but W:tA is not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not. I never read that ancestor spirits are the spirits of the dead. In 2nd Edition, Past Lives was still around and Ancestors was not. Back then, the 1st Edition Stargazer TB made a big deal about the Stargazer souls being reborn into other tribes, because there weren't enough Stargazer offspring.<br /> <br /> Then, there is Ancestor spirits, that are per description disconnected garou (garou turned spirit for not returning into the material world for to long).<br /> <br /> All in all, it makes most sense, to me, to believe ancestor spirits are a combination of memories of the garou they represent, memories of those who were contemporary witness and possibly what later generations made the persons to be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T11:55:28-07:00","id":1382360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1381944-heroic-spirits-in-typemoon?p=1382359#post1382359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not. I never read that ancestor spirits are the spirits of the dead. In 2nd Edition, Past Lives was still around and Ancestors was not. Back then, the 1st Edition Stargazer TB made a big deal about the Stargazer souls being reborn into other tribes, because there weren't enough Stargazer offspring.<br /> <br /> Then, there is Ancestor spirits, that are per description disconnected garou (garou turned spirit for not returning into the material world for to long).<br /> <br /> All in all, it makes most sense, to me, to believe ancestor spirits are a combination of memories of the garou they represent, memories of those who were contemporary witness and possibly what later generations made the persons to be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ancestors did replace Past Lives, though, and the reason cited was because Past Lives, as a name, didn't reflect what the Background was supposed to represent, making the Stargazer tribebook of 2e the odd one out. The game also says in a text box that Gaia might not have the importance that Garou ascribe to her, and then proceeds to ignore that at every turn where one of the Fera might contend with it, so the impression that I had was of the &quot;alternative&quot; being a kind of wiggle room space for optional campaigns, which the printed material never bothered to acknowledge. Hence, I advocate for a completely unironic take on those elements.<br /> <br /> (Aside: The ancestor-spirits that result from disconnected Garou and Fera seem like they would support ancestor-spirits being the actual, literal person they were after life, too.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}